From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] aic_load_fw: no rx refill after the bus has stopped

Seen on the 8 GiB board, 2026-09-24, in
`journalctl -b -p err` of a normal boot with the radio up:
  usb_err:<aicwf_usb_rx_submit_all_urb,311>: bus is not up=0
The same text appeared in two other logs: the 6 GiB board's cold-start
series of 2026-09-21 (506 ms after `aicwf_usb_disconnect enter`) and the vendor's own 6.6.98-aw2511
system on the eMMC. It does
not come on every boot.

Code says (aic_load_fw, pinned tag plus the earlier patches of this series; kernel 6.18.36):
- After the firmware upload the part leaves the bus to come back under its
  loaded id. Its rx URBs complete with errors as it drops off, and whatever
  is left the USB core terminates before it calls ->disconnect
  (drivers/usb/core/driver.c:455-458, usb_disable_interface() ->
  usb_hcd_flush_endpoint(), -ESHUTDOWN). So every rx URB is given back before
  ->disconnect, and each completion queues rx_urb_work (aicwf_usb.c:235)
  while the bus is still up; the work finds app_cmp set and returns (:314).
  On a boot that is 20 `app_cmp` lines, 75 us apart, before
  `aicwf_usb_disconnect enter`.
- The hub event and the refill work run in the same per-CPU worker pool
  (usb_hub_wq and system_percpu_wq are both per-CPU; the completions come
  from the same host controller's bottom half). The pool starts no second
  worker while one is running (kernel/workqueue.c:941-944, :3427-3430). If
  the hub worker gets the CPU back before the worker woken for the last
  refill, that refill stays pending while aicwf_usb_disconnect() ->
  aicwf_bus_deinit() busy-waits 500 ms (aic_txrxif.c:96, mdelay; the pool's
  CPU-intensive escape is 1 s on this board, workqueue.c:7948-7953 with
  lpj 96000) and aicwf_usb_bus_stop() sets USB_DOWN_ST (aicwf_usb.c:740).
  The refill runs at the hub worker's next sleep, finds the bus down and
  prints through usb_err() = pr_err (:311). Who wins the CPU is the race:
  some boots.
- The vendor cancels the work only in aicwf_usb_deinit() (:746), after the
  bus has been stopped and the 500 ms are over.
- The probe's own error path stops the bus with rx URBs still in flight: the
  reboot of a part already at its loaded id (rwnx_send_reboot, :1851), of a
  part below high speed (system_reboot, :1842), and a failed configuration or
  upload (:1855, :1859). The stop kills them
  (:741 -> :726), and both error branches of aicwf_usb_rx_complete() (:228,
  :235) queue a refill without the state check its data branch makes (:239):
  the same print again.

In the vendor driver: stopping the bus does not retire the rx refill, so
a refill queued while the bus was up can run after it is down, and URBs the
stop itself kills ask for another one. The work then reports the intended
state as an error. An earlier patch of this series keeps failure prints loud so that the log tells a dead
radio from a working one; this line breaks that on a working radio.

What changes:
- aicwf_usb_bus_stop() cancels a refill that is still pending before it sets
  USB_DOWN_ST. On the disconnect path nothing can queue a new one after that:
  every rx URB was given back before ->disconnect, and a refill would not
  resubmit anyway (app_cmp).
- Both error branches of the completion queue a refill only in USB_UP_ST, the
  data branch's rule, so URBs the stop kills queue none.
The print is not touched and keeps its level. On a bus that is up nothing
changes; a refill withheld on a stopped bus would have done nothing but print.
What is left: on the probe error path, a completion in the few instructions
between the cancel and the state change still queues a refill, which then runs
during the kill and prints this line, or "usb state is not up!" (:271) and "usb
rx refill fail" (:321) if it straddles the change. The disconnect path has no
such window: no URB is left there to complete.

Not taken, and why:
- cancel_work_sync() after the state change, as suggested in a bug report: a
  pending refill that gets the CPU in between prints. The stop sleeps there
  on the probe error path (killing live URBs). Before the state change, a
  refill that still runs finds the bus up; on the disconnect path it then
  returns at app_cmp.
- flush_work() instead of cancel: it runs the pending refill, which on the
  probe error path (app_cmp not yet set) resubmits the URBs the stop is
  about to kill.
- msleep() for the mdelay(500): the pending refill would usually run in the
  500 ms, but nothing guarantees it. The delay is the vendor's and unexplained;
  it stays. It is not what opens the race: two older copies in the tag have no
  delay there, and their stop follows the flush without a sleep in between
  just the same.
- No refill on -ENOENT/-ECONNRESET/-ESHUTDOWN, the usual completion idiom, or
  on any negative status, the shape our aic8800_fdrv uses
  (aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_usb.c:344, :423): a refill queued for any other status
  (a transaction error while the part drops off the bus) is starved the same
  way, and the second form also drops the refill after a transient error on a
  live bus.

Cross-read in the pinned tag: all seven copies of aic_load_fw/aicwf_usb.c
(ours and six under src/USB/patch/) carry the same completion and the same
stop, and two older aic8800_fdrv copies there the same logic; the aic8800_fdrv
copies of the SDIO and PCIe trees queue the refill from both error branches
the same way. No copy fixes it. Our aic8800_fdrv does not hit it: it refills
inside the completion with no work item, returns on `urb->status < 0` without
a refill, its bus stop kills no URBs (:2008), and aicwf_bus_deinit() kills
them after the stop (aicwf_txrxif.c:217). Its zero-length and oversized
branches do refill without a state check; a zero-length completion on a
stopped bus would print its own "bus is not up" (AICWFDBG LOGERROR =
KERN_WARNING, :885, msg-in copy :954). No log in this tree has that line. Left
alone.

Diagnostics under /sys/module/aic_load_fw/parameters:
- rx_loader_refill_cancelled (0444) counts refills still pending when the bus
  stopped; on the disconnect path each one is a refill the vendor code would
  have left to run after the stop.
- rx_loader_refill_skipped (0444) counts completions on a stopped bus that
  queued no refill (the probe error path).
- rx_loader_inject_pending_refill (0644), the stimulus: the next N disconnects
  queue the refill from the hub worker right before aicwf_bus_deinit(), which
  leaves it pending through the busy-wait -- the state the race produces on
  its own. It has to be armed before the loader loads, i.e. on the kernel
  command line. The race by itself is rare on our kernel: one line in 43
  boots of the 8 GiB board's console log, none in 24 cold boots of the
  default image.

Falsifier, on the board:
1. With `aic_load_fw.rx_loader_inject_pending_refill=1` on the command line, a
   build that carries only the stimulus prints the line on (almost) every
   boot, about 500 ms after `aicwf_usb_disconnect enter`: the refill runs at
   the hub worker's first sleep after the stop. If that worker reaches the
   vendor's late cancel without sleeping, the refill is swallowed and the boot
   shows nothing -- a stimulus miss, not evidence either way. With this patch
   no boot prints it, rx_loader_refill_cancelled reads 1 and
   rx_loader_refill_skipped 0. The stimulus reads 0 afterwards in both, so it
   fired.
2. Without the stimulus, cold boots with this patch print no line, and wl0 and
   both modules are there on every boot.
One boot with the line and this patch refutes it.

Assisted-by: Claude

diff --git a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicwf_usb.c b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicwf_usb.c
index c43fd3f..8d31a5f 100644
--- a/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicwf_usb.c
+++ b/src/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic_load_fw/aicwf_usb.c
@@ -211,6 +211,32 @@ static void aicwf_usb_tx_complete(struct urb *urb)
     spin_unlock_irqrestore(&usb_dev->tx_flow_lock, flags);
     }
 
+static uint rx_loader_refill_cancelled;
+module_param(rx_loader_refill_cancelled, uint, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(rx_loader_refill_cancelled, "refill work still pending when the bus stopped, cancelled instead of run");
+static uint rx_loader_refill_skipped;
+module_param(rx_loader_refill_skipped, uint, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(rx_loader_refill_skipped, "rx completions on a stopped bus that did not queue the refill work");
+static int rx_loader_inject_pending_refill;
+module_param(rx_loader_inject_pending_refill, int, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(rx_loader_inject_pending_refill, "Test stimulus: the next N disconnects queue the rx refill before they stop the bus");
+
+/* No refill work may run once the bus is down: it would only find
+ * USB_DOWN_ST in aicwf_usb_rx_submit_all_urb() and report it as an error.
+ * aicwf_usb_bus_stop() cancels a refill that is still pending before it sets
+ * USB_DOWN_ST, and a URB completing after that (the stop kills the rx URBs)
+ * queues none -- the rule the data branch of aicwf_usb_rx_complete() already
+ * follows.
+ */
+static void aicwf_usb_rx_refill(struct aic_usb_dev *usb_dev)
+{
+    if (usb_dev->state != USB_UP_ST) {
+        rx_loader_refill_skipped++;
+        return;
+    }
+    schedule_work(&usb_dev->rx_urb_work);
+}
+
 static void aicwf_usb_rx_complete(struct urb *urb)
 {
     struct aicwf_usb_buf *usb_buf = (struct aicwf_usb_buf *) urb->context;
@@ -225,14 +251,14 @@ static void aicwf_usb_rx_complete(struct urb *urb)
     if (urb->actual_length > urb->transfer_buffer_length) {
         aicwf_dev_skb_free(skb);
         aicwf_usb_rx_buf_put(usb_dev, usb_buf);
-        schedule_work(&usb_dev->rx_urb_work);
+        aicwf_usb_rx_refill(usb_dev);
         return;
     }
 
     if (urb->status != 0 || !urb->actual_length) {
         aicwf_dev_skb_free(skb);
         aicwf_usb_rx_buf_put(usb_dev, usb_buf);
-        schedule_work(&usb_dev->rx_urb_work);
+        aicwf_usb_rx_refill(usb_dev);
         return;
     }
 
@@ -737,6 +763,9 @@ static void aicwf_usb_bus_stop(struct device *dev)
     if (usb_dev->state == USB_DOWN_ST)
         return;
 
+    /* Before USB_DOWN_ST, see aicwf_usb_rx_refill(). */
+    if (cancel_work_sync(&usb_dev->rx_urb_work))
+        rx_loader_refill_cancelled++;
     aicwf_usb_state_change(usb_dev, USB_DOWN_ST);
     aicwf_usb_cancel_all_urbs(usb_dev);
 }
@@ -1888,6 +1917,14 @@ static void aicwf_usb_disconnect(struct usb_interface *intf)
     if (!usb_dev)
         return;
 
+    /* Stimulus: a refill queued here, from the hub worker that is about to
+     * busy-wait and stop the bus, stays pending until that worker sleeps --
+     * the state the race leaves behind on some boots.
+     */
+    if (unlikely(rx_loader_inject_pending_refill > 0) && usb_dev->state == USB_UP_ST) {
+        rx_loader_inject_pending_refill--;
+        schedule_work(&usb_dev->rx_urb_work);
+    }
     aicwf_bus_deinit(usb_dev->dev);
     aicwf_usb_deinit(usb_dev);
     if (usb_dev->rx_priv)
